      "text": "[id=A1]\nAppendix A Benchmark Details\n[id=A1.SS1]\nA.1 Safety Benchmarks\n[id=A1.I1.i1] •\n[id=A1.I1.i1.p1.1] StrongREJECT (Souly et al., 2024): 313 prompts across six harm categories, evaluated using the StrongREJECT fine-tuned evaluator to produce compliance scores in [0,1][0,1].\n[id=A1.I1.i2] •\n[id=A1.I1.i2.p1.1] Sorry-Bench (Xie et al., 2025): 450 prompts spanning 45 fine-grained safety categories, evaluated using a fine-tuned Mistral-7B judge.\n[id=A1.I1.i3] •\n[id=A1.I1.i3.p1.1] JailbreakBench (Chao et al., 2024): 100 harmful prompts, evaluated using LlamaGuard-3-8B.\n[id=A1.I1.i4] •\n[id=A1.I1.i4.p1.1] HarmBench Validation (Mazeika et al., 2024): 100 prompts from the HarmBench validation set, evaluated using LlamaGuard-3-8B.\n[id=A1.I1.i5] •\n[id=A1.I1.i5.p1.1] AdvBench (Zou et al., 2023a): 520 harmful prompts, evaluated using LlamaGuard-3-8B.\n[id=A1.SS2]\nA.2 Utility Benchmarks\n[id=A1.I2.i1] •\n[id=A1.I2.i1.p1.1] MMLU (Hendrycks et al., 2021): 57-subject multiple-choice knowledge benchmark.\n[id=A1.I2.i2] •\n[id=A1.I2.i2.p1.1] HellaSwag (Zellers et al., 2019): Commonsense reasoning via sentence completion.\n[id=A1.I2.i3] •\n[id=A1.I2.i3.p1.1] WinoGrande (Sakaguchi et al., 2021): Commonsense reasoning via pronoun resolution.\n[id=A1.I2.i4] •\n[id=A1.I2.i4.p1.1] GSM8K (Cobbe et al., 2021): Grade-school math word problems.\n[id=A1.I2.i5] •\n[id=A1.I2.i5.p1.1] TruthfulQA (Lin et al., 2022): Factual accuracy under adversarial prompting.\n[id=A1.I2.i6] •\n[id=A1.I2.i6.p1.1] IFEval (Zhou et al., 2023): Instruction-following evaluation.\n[id=A1.SS3]\nA.3 Detailed safety and utility benchmark results\n[id=A1.SS3.p1.1] Table 1 shows detailed safety and utility benchmark results for all models and their GRP‑Oblit and GRP‑Oblit-1 unaligned, TwinBreak unaligned and Abliteration unaligned variants.\nTable 1: Comprehensive benchmark results across all models and techniques. Bold indicates best technique per model for each benchmark. Utility metrics: hig